---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Sheet from '../components/Sheet.astro'
import PageToolbar from '../components/PageToolbar.astro'
import '../styles/legal.css'

/*
 * Terms. Written against what the code actually does, not a template:
 * anyone can read without an account, posting needs a magic-link sign-in,
 * Challenges are public the moment they are posted, and the stage field is
 * limited to the author or an admin (apps/api/src/index.ts).
 */
const updated = '11 September 2026'
---
<Base
  title="Terms - Techno Optimists"
  description="The rules for posting, contributing and using Techno Optimists."
>
  <Sheet>
    <PageToolbar label="Terms" />
    <main class="legal-page">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <h1>Terms of use</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Who runs this</h2>
        <p>
          Techno Optimists is operated by Techguyver Labs, LLC, a Delaware limited
          liability company. Contact: <a href="mailto:roy@techguyverlabs.org">roy@techguyverlabs.org</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the site is</h2>
        <p>
          A community built to connect people who want to understand real-world Challenges
          and help each other make things better. There is no business model in place;
          the focus is useful connections and collaboration. Reading needs
          no account. Posting a Challenge, adding progress or using a typed action needs
          you to sign in with your email address.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Open source and contributing</h2>
        <p>
          The site's code is <a href="https://github.com/royherma/techno-optimists">open source</a>
          under the <a href="https://github.com/royherma/techno-optimists/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>.
          You are welcome to suggest improvements, report bugs and submit pull requests.
          See <a href="/contribute">how to contribute</a> for ways to help, with or without code.
        </p>
        <p>
          The code license does not automatically apply to members' Challenges, comments
          or uploads. You keep ownership of your contributions. Agree directly with
          collaborators on permission to reuse their work and on any shared ownership,
          credit, costs or payment before starting work together.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contributing code does not grant access to member accounts, private data or
          administration of this site. Maintainers review proposed changes before they
          become part of the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What you post</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of what you write and upload. By posting you give us
          permission to display it on the site and in links that point to it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything you post to a Challenge is public from the moment you post it. Your
          handle is shown next to it. Do not post anything you are not free to share -
          someone else's private information, work you have no right to publish, or
          material that is illegal where you are.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you describe someone else's problem rather than your own, say where the
          account came from. The site records a source alongside the Challenge for
          exactly this.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Working on someone's Challenge</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone signed in can add progress, ideas and comments to any Challenge. Moving
          a Challenge through its lifecycle stages is limited to the person who posted
          it, and to administrators. Editorial changes to Challenge titles, summaries
          and descriptions, and bulk imports, are limited to administrators.
        </p>
        <p>
          Advice on this site comes from other members, not from us. Nothing here is
          professional engineering, medical, legal or safety advice. Work involving
          electricity, water supplies, structures, chemicals, vehicles or food carries
          real risk, and you are responsible for what you build and test.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we can do</h2>
        <p>
          We can remove content or close an account that breaks these terms, without
          notice where the content is harmful. You can close your own account at any
          time from your account page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as it is. We do not promise it will be available,
          correct, or fit for a particular purpose, and to the extent the law allows we
          are not liable for loss arising from your use of it or from anything you build
          based on what you read here.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms will change as the site does. The date at the top is when this
          version was published.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="legal-footer-link">
        See also <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
  </Sheet>
</Base>
